# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TDAI global images local deployment - environment variable template
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # Edit .env, replacing REPLACE_ME with your own values
#   ./start-all.sh
#
# Two independent parameter groups:
#   MEMORY_*   → used by memory + memory-hub (LLM for internal memory/knowledge services)
#   PROXY_*    → used by proxy (upstream LLM that user requests are forwarded to)
# The two groups can be identical, or point to completely different models/providers.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Image tags ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to public Docker Hub images (multi-arch amd64 + arm64, no login needed):
#   https://hub.docker.com/r/agentmemory/memory-core
#   https://hub.docker.com/r/agentmemory/memory-proxy
#   https://hub.docker.com/r/agentmemory/memory-hub
# To pin a version, replace :latest with a specific version, e.g. :1.0.0-beta.1.
# Note: if a local :latest image with the same name already exists, the script
# reuses it directly and will not automatically detect remote updates.
# To pull the newest version, use `PULL=1 ./start-all.sh`.
MEMORY_CORE_IMAGE=agentmemory/memory-core:latest
MEMORY_HUB_IMAGE=agentmemory/memory-hub:latest
PROXY_IMAGE=agentmemory/memory-proxy:latest

# ── Tencent intranet alternative (for internal colleagues) ───────────────────
# Internal environments (Tencent office network / devcloud) can override these
# to the mirrors.tencent.com private registry, avoiding the public Docker Hub.
# Run `docker login mirrors.tencent.com` before use.
# MEMORY_CORE_IMAGE=mirrors.tencent.com/memory-team-control/memory-core:latest
# MEMORY_HUB_IMAGE=mirrors.tencent.com/memory-team-control/memory-hub:latest
# PROXY_IMAGE=mirrors.tencent.com/memory-team-control/proxy:latest

# ── memory group: LLM called internally by memory + memory-hub ───────────────
# Purpose: embed/summarize in memory; wiki ingest / summarization for knowledge in memory-hub
MEMORY_LLM_BASE_URL=REPLACE_ME              # e.g. https://api.deepseek.com/v1
MEMORY_LLM_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME               # e.g. sk-xxxxxxxx
MEMORY_LLM_MODEL=REPLACE_ME                 # e.g. deepseek-chat
MEMORY_LLM_PROTOCOL=openai                  # openai | anthropic

# ── proxy group: upstream LLM that proxy forwards user requests to ───────────
# Purpose: coding agents / clients call proxy:8096, and proxy forwards to this upstream
PROXY_UPSTREAM_URL=REPLACE_ME               # e.g. https://api.deepseek.com/v1
PROXY_UPSTREAM_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME           # e.g. sk-xxxxxxxx (can differ from the memory group)
PROXY_UPSTREAM_MODEL=REPLACE_ME             # e.g. deepseek-chat

# ── Ports (defaults work out of the box; change here on local conflicts) ─────
MEMORY_CORE_PORT=8420
PANEL_PORT=8125
KNOWLEDGE_PORT=8424
PROXY_PORT=8096

# ── knowledge externally reachable address (required by memory-hub) ──────────
# Lets agents / gateway reach the KS tools API. Must include the /v3 prefix.
# For local setups, defaults to host.docker.internal so containers can loop back to the host.
KNOWLEDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8424/v3

# ── Base URL shown in the Panel UI "client connection address" card (open-source local deployment only)
# In open-source deployments, core and proxy run separately; coding agent clients
# connect to the proxy, not core/gateway.
# This value is only used by the Panel UI for display (e.g. the baseUrl copy cards
# for CodeBuddy / ClaudeCode). Panel backend → Kernel forwarding always goes through
# REMOTE_INSTANCE_URL (=memory-core) and is unaffected by this variable.
#
# When unset, the script auto-detects the host LAN IP (`hostname -I` / macOS
# `ipconfig getifaddr en0`) and builds `http://<lan-ip>:${PROXY_PORT}` — other
# computers can connect directly by copying the URL from the card.
# Explicitly setting it empty (="") falls back to the old gateway_endpoint behavior.
# To set it explicitly (e.g. a public domain / specific NIC IP), uncomment the line below and fill in a real value:
# MEMORY_HUB_PROXY_PUBLIC_URL=http://192.168.1.100:8096

# ── Data volume names ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MEMORY_CORE_VOLUME=tdai-memory-core-data
PANEL_VOLUME=tdai-panel-data

# ── memory-core internal credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Gateway Bearer-layer admin credential.
#   Empty (default) — disables the Bearer gate (zero-config local experience; the
#                     proxy's auth/sessionInit can only connect directly to
#                     memory-core under this configuration; see the top comments
#                     in start-memory-core.sh)
#   Non-empty       — all requests must carry `Authorization: Bearer <key>`; the
#                     proxy currently does not send this header, so the proxy's
#                     auth/sessionInit will fail
# Production environments should only enable a non-empty key after the proxy side is fixed.
MEMORY_CORE_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# admin username (for first-time init-admin). The user_key is auto-generated as a
# random sk-mem- key on first startup and stored in ./.admin-key — subsequent
# scripts / claude-proxy read from that file; no manual entry needed.
MEMORY_CORE_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
